feat(transcripts): record every fleet ship's full conversation, surface in dashboard + CLI

New lib/transcripts.ts owns one fleet_transcripts row per spawn with
child fleet_transcript_messages + fleet_transcript_outputs tables. The
spawner now records start/messages/finalize transparently when a
transcripts dep is provided; existing call sites that don't pass one
keep their current behavior (back-compat).

Surfaces:
- pd transcripts list / show / watch / cost / delete (cli/commands/transcripts.ts)
- /transcripts*, /transcripts/stream (SSE) routes
- Fleet Transcripts panel in the dashboard with live SSE updates and a
  cost rollup header

Security:
- Common secret patterns (API_KEY=, Bearer, gh*_, sk-, sk-ant-, stripe,
  AWS AKIA) scrubbed from message content and tool-call args before
  storage. Last 4 chars preserved for audit reference.
- Tool-call string fields > 10KB truncated to 1KB + sha256 hash.
- DELETE gated by destructive-confirm at the CLI layer.

NOTE: server.ts wiring is intentionally NOT in this commit. server.ts is
currently claimed by another in-flight session (cockpit-phase-2-commit).
The wiring is a 3-line additive change (import createTranscripts,
instantiate transcripts module, add to deps). It will land in a follow-up
once the cockpit session merges, OR can be cherry-picked into the
cockpit branch by that agent. Without this wiring, /transcripts returns
501 - the new module exists but is dormant.

Tests: 47 new (transcripts unit 31, transcripts routes 12, spawner
integration 4). 170 total in related suites pass. tsc clean.


